module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.product_value_at_a_scalar_formal_is_accepted

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data product_value_at_a_scalar_formal_is_accepted: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "product_value_at_a_scalar_formal_is_accepted" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a value whose type is a nominal PRODUCT (a record) reaches a position whose declared type is a kernel scalar, or a where-refinement of one such as std.types EpochMs (`Int where range(min: 0)`), and the program is Accepted on the seed path. HARM: silent wrongness at the compiler floor. DESIGN section 4b names `values inhabit declared types` as part of the ordinary floor, so this sits below it, not on a rung: the record fails, if at all, inside a scalar primitive at run time, or orders an event by a value that is not a time.",

    "HOW IT SURFACED (bright-wolf-485, gunbc#13242's forged-probe census): a gunbc.machine_intake_bmc_secure ControllerClockReading -- `type ControllerClockReading { reported_millis: EpochMs, evidence: EvidenceRef }`, a controller's own clock, never an ordering clock -- passed as the argument read_at_millis of dry_read_bmc_account_state, declared `read_at_millis: EpochMs`, drew no blocking refusal. It is NOT a nominal/structural confusion: EpochMs is a refinement of the kernel Int and shares no shape with a record. It is NOT a harness defect: the harness control below refuses on the same route.",

    "REPRODUCTION, independent of machine_intake, measured on main 864c9ce0c9 on the seed, by two routes in one remote dispatch each. ROUTE ONE, an entry compile (`gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --source-root <probe dir> --entry <probe> --target dag --output-dir <dir>`): with `type Reading { reported_millis: EpochMs, evidence: String }` and `fn take(read_at_millis: EpochMs) -> EpochMs`, the call `take(read_at_millis: r)` for `r: Reading` exits 0. So does the same record at a locally declared `type Ms = Int where range(min: 0)` formal, at an EpochMs declared return (`fn probe(r: Reading) -> EpochMs { r }`), and at a plain Int formal. HARNESS CONTROL: `take(b: i)` with `i: Int` at `b: Bool` exits 1 with `value does not inhabit its declared type at the direct call argument for parameter 'b'`. POSITIVE CONTROL: `take(read_at_millis: r.reported_millis)` exits 0. ROUTE TWO, the compile-diagnostic census harness the forged-probe witnesses use (claim_batch over test.claim.declared_type_product_at_kernel_scalar_formal_witness_test): the three reds FAIL (no blocking DeclaredTypeNotInhabited), and the positive and harness controls PASS. The two routes agree.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: TWO ARMS, and the specimen's arm is the quieter one. (1) REFINEMENT FORMAL, the EpochMs specimen: no inhabitance diagnostic at all, only the unrelated advisory `where-refinement unenforced: predicate 'range' on 'Product(EpochMs)'`. Read from v1.compiler.infer declared_type_inhabitance, every arm declines: record_at_scalar_needs_identity wants a declared head exposed as a kernel scalar and a refinement is not exposed as one; refinement_inhabitance answers only when BOTH sides carry a refinement chain and an unrefined record carries none; kernel_value_declared_type_mismatch exits because the produced value is not a kernel; nominal_product_inhabitance_refusal names no declared head because a refinement is not a Conj product. The pair reaches the terminal Inhabits by fallthrough -- the same shape as gunbc.recurring_failure_mode declared_type_wall_keyed_on_the_value_being_a_kernel specimen three, a pair judged by no arm. (2) PLAIN KERNEL FORMAL: record_at_scalar_needs_identity answers UndecidableProducedIdentityErased, the counted advisory DeclaredTypeInhabitanceUndecided. That arm was introduced on purpose by gunbc#9706 and is recorded in docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md as the direct-call record-to-scalar row, with a rationale that is historical and not re-established here (see the boundary receipt): a blocking arm exposed compiler-source sites whose produced identity could not be recovered at the binding edge, and the homonym pair std.types FilePath (a String refinement) and v2.extdeps.file_system FilePath (a record) made a bare-head answer a guess. test.claim.declared_type_inhabitance_direct_call_witness_test pins that advisory, and test.claim.sole_constructor_type_head_exposure_witness_test sealed_carrier_at_kernel_formal_refuses already carries a sealed-carrier specimen of arm (2) in v2.workflow.floor_expected_red. No recurring_failure_mode row existed for either arm. (3) SEED-ONLY BY READING, NOT BY MEASUREMENT: v2.std.inhabitance declared_type_inhabitance_structural compares the pair by exact structural equality and admits a produced value only through ITS OWN declared refinement carrier, so a record at EpochMs reaches exact_refusal. v2 was not executed on this fixture.",

    "THE EARLIEST UNJUSTIFIED BOUNDARY (DESIGN section 6b), one per arm. For arm (1) it is the refinement seam: a where-refinement's base carrier is a modeled fact (where_refinement_chain names it), but declared_type_inhabitance never judges a refined declared type against an UNREFINED produced value by that base -- refinement_inhabitance returns no answer instead of handing the pair to the base, so no downstream arm judges it. For arm (2) it is the arm itself: record_at_scalar_needs_identity already reads expected_type_head_exposure for BOTH nodes, and that exposure already establishes a kernel-scalar head on one side and a product head on the other, yet the arm selects InhabitanceUndecidable rather than a refusal. gunbc#9706's rationale -- that the binding edge does not carry the produced value's declaration identity -- is HISTORICAL: it explains why the advisory was introduced, it is not established at this snapshot, and it is superseded/unverified here, because the declaration-keyed exposure the arm consults already exists. Repairing (1) alone moves the specimen from silent to arm (2)'s counted advisory, not to a refusal; the refusal needs both.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder -- arm (1) silently wrong, arm (2) counted by a non-blocking advisory. CEILING: structurally guaranteed. Both identities are established in the modeled facts, a product never inhabits a kernel scalar or a refinement of one, and the invalid program is authorable in source, so impossibility is not available. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, named as the capability: the seed's declared-type inhabitance judges a product against a scalar formal from the existing resolved type-head exposure at every declared-type position -- record_at_scalar_needs_identity re-derived to refuse DeclaredTypeNotInhabited when that exposure establishes a product against a kernel scalar, AND a refined declared type judged through its base carrier when the produced value is unrefined. No new identity producer is part of this capability. SUFFICIENT FOR: all three enrolled reds in test.claim.declared_type_product_at_kernel_scalar_formal_witness_test to refuse, the positive control and a refined value at its own base to stay accepted, and the whole-corpus census of newly refused sites to be dispositioned. A spelling check or a per-name exemption is not this capability. OWNER: none yet.",

    "CLIMBED (gunbc#13391) to structurally guaranteed at the seed. v1.compiler.infer record_at_scalar_needs_identity, which declined with UndecidableProducedIdentityErased, is deleted; product_at_scalar_declared_type refuses RefusedProductAtScalar, a blocking DeclaredTypeNotInhabited. Both heads are read from expected_type_head_exposure, which is keyed on the declaring file plus name of the RESOLVED declaration, so the produced identity at the binding edge is the declaration identity gunbc#9706 found missing when that judgment read a bare head -- the FilePath homonym pair is two census keys, not one spelling. The refinement seam is closed by declared_head_is_kernel_scalar_through_refinement, which peels a where-refined declared type through where_refinement_chain to its base before asking for a kernel head. The same pair is handed to declared_type_obligation_diags from declared_type_conformance_diags_core, so the declared-return, let, data and record-field positions are judged by the one relation the direct-call argument uses. EVIDENCE: the three test.claim.declared_type_product_at_kernel_scalar_formal_witness_test reds and test.claim.sole_constructor_type_head_exposure_witness_test sealed_carrier_at_kernel_formal_refuses PASS and leave v2.workflow.floor_expected_red; they stay enrolled as permanent regression controls (DESIGN 4b(4)). The positive control (the record's EpochMs field at an EpochMs formal) and test.claim.declared_type_inhabitance_direct_call_witness_test w_a_branded_refinement_at_its_own_declared_base_inhabits stay green. RESIDUAL: a produced value that is itself a where-refinement of a product exposes OpaqueTypeHead and is not judged by this arm; that pair belongs to gunbc.recurring_failure_mode absence_classifier_default_bucket.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "declared_type_inhabitance", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "refinement_inhabitance", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "product_at_scalar_declared_type", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.declared_type_product_at_kernel_scalar_formal_witness_test", decl_name: "a_record_at_an_epoch_ms_argument_refuses", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.declared_type_product_at_kernel_scalar_formal_witness_test", decl_name: "the_harness_refuses_an_int_at_a_bool_argument", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
